{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Send for yourself men.</b> Why is the section of the spies juxtaposed to the section of Miriam? Because she was punished on account of the matter of slander — she spoke against her brother — and these wicked men saw and did not take instruction (Tanchuma)." "<b>Send for yourself.</b> At your discretion — I am not commanding you; if you wish, send. For Israel came and said, ״נִשְׁלְחָה אֲנָשִׁים לְפָנֵינוּ״, as it says ״וַתִּקְרְבוּן אֵלַי כֻּלְּכֶם״ etc. (Deuteronomy 1), and Moses consulted the Shechinah. He said: I told them it is good, as it says ״אַעֲלֶה אֶתְכֶם מֵעֳנִי מִצְרַיִם״ etc. (Exodus 3) — by their lives, I give them room to stumble in the matter of spies, so that they not inherit it (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:39.241252746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}